  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="64d5-0511-e654-4303" name="Kingdom of Hungary (Vlad the Impaler) - List Notes" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false">
      <description>KINGDOM OF HUNGARY (Vlad the Impaler, pp.12-16): Hungarian armies of the Arpad and Angevin eras, the Period of the New Men (Hunyadi and Corvinus) and Hungarian/Crusader armies, 1280-1526. Special rules from the book: Allies and Mercenaries rule, Crusader, Arrogant Pride, Mixed Order, German Wedge, Veteran. Allies and mercenaries from other lists are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Kingdom of Hungary - Arpad &amp; Angevin (1280-1441)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%, at least 33%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  ARPAD &amp; ANGEVIN ERAS, 1280-1441. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry 33-75% (all cavalry choices except Serbian Hussars); Infantry and Artillery up to 50% (Honvéd, Nyílpuska, Crossbowmen and Elöcsatározó; 0-1 Heavy Ágyú (Heavy Bombard) per 2,000 points, only after 1380, no other Bombard choices; 0-1 Katapulta (Mangonel) per 1,000 pts); Mercenaries and Allies up to 25% (Serbia 1280-1441, Moldavia 1359-1441, Walachia 1330-1441, Bulgaria until 1396, Albania 1280-1441, Italian Condotta from Armies of Chivalry; documented only; no Armigeri).
[Kingdom of Hungary - Period of the New Men (1441-1526)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  THE PERIOD OF THE NEW MEN, 1441-1526. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry up to 50% (all cavalry choices available); Infantry and Artillery 25-75% (all infantry and artillery choices available; 0-1 War wagon per every 1,000 pts; 0-1 Ágyú (Bombard) or Katapulta (Mangonel) per every 650 pts; 0-1 Wagon tabor, no more than one wagon per 1,000 points); Mercenaries and Allies up to 25%, as Armigeri and from Serbia (until 1458), Moldavia (until 1527), Walachia (until 1508), Albania (Stradioti only until 1468), Italian Condotta (documented only). See special character Mátyás Corvinus for making a Black Army.
[Kingdom of Hungary - Hungarian-Crusader (1396, 1443-8, 1456)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Crusaders: up to 50%, at least 25%
  HUNGARIAN/CRUSADER ARMIES, 1396, 1443-8, 1456. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 25% (all cavalry choices); Infantry and Artillery up to 25% (all choices; 0-1 War wagon per every 1,000 pts; 0-1 Ágyú (Bombard) or Katapulta (Mangonel) per every 650 pts; 0-1 Wagon tabor, no more than one wagon per 1,000 points); Crusaders 25-50% (must take one unit of Crusader Knights for every unit of Crusader Sergeants if Crusader cavalry is taken); Mercenaries and Allies up to 25% from Serbia (until 1458), Moldavia, Walachia, Bulgaria (until 1396), Albania (Stradioti only), Italian Condotta (documented only; no Armigeri).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
